# Build
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose. Without the leading slash these match a
# directory of that name at any depth, and patches/webrtc/build/ is one:
# the patch documented in docs/webrtc-toolchain.md as
# build/0001-libstdcxx-and-crel-opt-outs.patch was never committed because
# `git add` refused it silently. scripts/build_webrtc.sh passes the two GN
# arguments that patch declares, so a clone that has never seen the file
# fails at gn gen, and the Linux media layer builds only on machines where
# it happens to exist untracked.
/build/
/out/
/install/
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Dependencies
# The contents rather than the directory itself, because git cannot re-include
# anything under a directory it was told to exclude.
third_party/*
# Vendored source, not a downloaded dependency: nvEncodeAPI.h is a 300 KB MIT
# header with its provenance recorded next to it, and a checkout without it
# cannot build the NVENC encoder at all.
!third_party/nvcodec/
vcpkg_installed/
.cache/

# The database tool, when it is built in place rather than with `go run`.
tools/dbadmin/dbadmin

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local config and secrets
config.local.json
*.pem
*.key

# The pinned vcpkg checkout, created by scripts/ci_vcpkg.sh
.vcpkg/

# The install tree the Windows release procedure stages before windeployqt
# and cpack run over it. On a runner it disappears with the machine; on a
# development one it sits in the working tree looking like new source.
stage/
